CONSTANT: π
Type: real transcendental
SID: S    PED: Q    RDG: PhaseOp
Operators:
  π = C / d                          (C = circumference, d = diameter)
  π = 4 Σ_{n=0}^∞ (-1)^n / (2n+1)
  ζ(2) = Σ_{n=1}^∞ 1/n² = π² / 6
  π/2 = ∏_{n=1}^∞ [ (2n)/(2n-1) * (2n)/(2n+1) ]
  ∫_{-∞}^∞ exp(-x²) dx = √π
  e^{iπ} + 1 = 0
Fundamentals: Euclidean geometry, Fourier analysis, Gaussian integrals

======================================================================
CONSTANT: e
Type: real transcendental
SID: S    PED: P    RDG: LinMap
Operators:
  e = lim_{n→∞} (1 + 1/n)^n
  e = Σ_{n=0}^∞ 1/n!
  d/dx (e^x) = e^x
  e = [2; 1,2,1, 1,4,1, 1,6,1, ...]
Fundamentals: unique solution to y' = y; continuous compounding

======================================================================
CONSTANT: i
Type: imaginary algebraic
SID: I    PED: Q    RDG: PhaseOp
Operators:
  i² = -1
  multiplication by i = rotation by π/2 in complex plane
  e^{iθ} = cos θ + i sin θ
Fundamentals: complex rotation generator

======================================================================
CONSTANT: φ
Type: real algebraic irrational
SID: S    PED: P    RDG: SimOp
Operators:
  φ = (1 + √5)/2
  φ² - φ - 1 = 0
  φ = 1 + 1/φ
  φ = [1; 1,1,1,...]
  lim_{n→∞} F_{n+1}/F_n = φ
Fundamentals: self-similarity fixed point, extreme-and-mean ratio

======================================================================
CONSTANT: √2
Type: real algebraic irrational
SID: S    PED: P    RDG: SimOp
Operators:
  positive root of x² - 2 = 0
  √2 = [1; 2,2,2,...]
  √2 = 1 + 1/(2 + 1/(2 + ...))
Fundamentals: diagonal of unit square

======================================================================
CONSTANT: ln 2
Type: real transcendental
SID: S    PED: P    RDG: LinMap
Operators:
  ln 2 = Σ_{n=1}^∞ (-1)^{n+1}/n
  ln 2 = ∫_1^2 (1/x) dx
Fundamentals: natural log of 2; binary entropy base

======================================================================
CONSTANT: τ
Type: real transcendental
SID: S    PED: Q    RDG: PhaseOp
Operators:
  τ = 2π
Fundamentals: full-circle constant (circumference/radius)

======================================================================
CONSTANT: e^π
Type: real transcendental
SID: S    PED: P    RDG: LinMap
Operators:
  e^π = exp(π)
  e^π = (-1)^{-i}
  Iteration: k_0 = 1/√2
             k_{n+1} = (1 - √(1-k_n²))/(1 + √(1-k_n²))
             (4/k_{n+1})^{2^{-n}} → e^π
Fundamentals: Gelfond–Schneider theorem

======================================================================
CONSTANT: γ
Type: real (irrationality open)
SID: I    PED: E    RDG: AsympOp
Operators:
  γ = lim_{n→∞} (H_n - ln n)
  γ = ∫_1^∞ (1/⌊x⌋ - 1/x) dx
  γ = -Γ'(1)
  γ = Σ_{k=2}^∞ (-1)^k ζ(k)/k
  1/Γ(z) = z exp(γ z) ∏_{n=1}^∞ (1 + z/n) exp(-z/n)
Fundamentals: harmonic–logarithmic asymptotic gap

======================================================================
CONSTANT: δ
Type: real (transcendence open)
SID: I    PED: P    RDG: RenormOp
Operators:
  δ = lim_{n→∞} (a_{n-1} - a_{n-2}) / (a_n - a_{n-1})
  where a_n are successive period-doubling bifurcation parameters
  for unimodal maps with quadratic maximum
Fundamentals: universal renormalization scaling ratio

======================================================================
CONSTANT: ζ(3)
Type: real irrational
SID: D    PED: E    RDG: DirichletOp
Operators:
  ζ(3) = Σ_{n=1}^∞ 1/n³
  ζ(3) = ∫_0^1 ∫_0^1 ∫_0^1 dx dy dz / (1 - x y z)
Fundamentals: Apéry's theorem (irrational); special zeta value

======================================================================
CONSTANT: G
Type: real (irrationality open)
SID: D    PED: E    RDG: DirichletOp
Operators:
  G = Σ_{n=0}^∞ (-1)^n / (2n+1)² = β(2)
  G = -∫_0^1 (ln t)/(1 + t²) dt
  G = (1/4) [ψ_1(1/4) - ψ_1(3/4)]
Fundamentals: Dirichlet beta at 2; ideal hyperbolic octahedron volume = 4G

======================================================================
CONSTANT: K₀
Type: real (status open)
SID: D    PED: E    RDG: DistribOp
Operators:
  For almost every x = [a0; a1,a2,...]:
    K₀ = lim_{n→∞} (a1 a2 ... an)^{1/n}
  K₀ = ∏_{r=1}^∞ [1 + 1/(r(r+2))]^{log_2 r}
Fundamentals: Khinchin's theorem (almost-everywhere continued-fraction mean)

======================================================================
CONSTANT: K
Type: real
SID: D    PED: E    RDG: DistribOp
Operators:
  K = lim_{n→∞} [ Σ_{k=1}^n r_2(k)/k - π ln n ]
  K = π (2 ln 2 + 3 ln π + 2γ - 4 ln Γ(1/4))
  K = π ln (4 π³ exp(2γ) / Γ(1/4)^4)
Fundamentals: asymptotic constant for sum-of-two-squares representation function

======================================================================
CONSTANT: C₂
Type: real
SID: D    PED: E    RDG: DistribOp
Operators:
  C₂ = ∏_{p≥3} (1 - 1/(p-1)²)
     = ∏_{p≥3} p(p-2)/(p-1)²
Fundamentals: Hardy–Littlewood singular series for twin primes
  conjectured π_2(x) ~ 2 C₂ ∫_2^x dt / (ln t)²

